  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-0.4)=-23.578\\,178{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248-{23.578}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-{23.578}^{\u2218}$ is not in the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ To get the first solution that's within the required domain, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-{23.578}^{\u2218}.$ To do this, we simply add ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{23.578}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={336.422}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={23.578}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={23.578}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/c587e119531c3363816f72e9f2e1acdcc1aba87f278caa658342cbff144b0dad.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{23.578}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={203.578}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248{204}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248{336}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
